# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for the optimistic reads of the shared map
# (D12; `tree/node/optimistic.rs`): a reader reads a node in place
# while a writer that holds it changes it, and a version check afterwards
# throws away what it read. Every entry names a reader-side function, so a
# race between two writers, which the latches forbid, is still reported.
race:shoal::detail::Racing
race:shoal::detail::RacingCopy
race:shoal::detail::NodeInlineKeys
race:shoal::detail::VectorCount
race:shoal::detail::NeonLanes
race:load_racing_header
race:load_racing_has_head
race:load_racing_shared_prefix
race:place_outside_racing
# The shared hash map's optimistic readers (`hash_map.hpp`): a shard's
# block, its tags and slots, read while a writer that holds the shard changes
# them, and checked against the shard's version after.
race:shoal::detail::InlineHashTable*::racing_view
race:shoal::detail::InlineHashTable*::racing_group
race:shoal::detail::InlineHashTable*::racing_hash
race:shoal::detail::InlineHashTable*::racing_find_from
race:shoal::detail::InlineHashTable*::RacingLookup
# A latch word is only ever accessed atomically, by `NodeLatch`, which reads
# and writes nothing else and calls nothing: a race reported inside it is with
# a non-atomic write to a latch word, a fresh page's zeroing by its allocator.
# A reader that reached the page through a racing edge read checks the latch
# with a relaxed load, whose value the compare-and-swap after it settles, or
# reads a version its parent's check throws away (D12).
race:shoal::detail::NodeLatch
